        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-West Germanic *watar 'water'",
          "to": "weter"
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-West Germanic *þak 'roof'",
          "to": "thek"
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-West Germanic *fader 'father'",
          "to": "feder"
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-West Germanic *lātan 'to let'",
          "to": "lēta",
          "note": "Anglo-Frisian brightening went further in Frisian than in English: short *a became e (Old English æ) and long *ā became ē (Old English ǣ); compare Old English fæst, glæs, wæter, lǣtan."
        }
